records and pill counts with electronic monitoring of adherence to antihypertensive therapy</article-title><source>Med Care</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>846</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10493464</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-ndt-3-117"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Claxton</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierce</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>A systematic review of the Associations between dose regimens and medication compliance</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>1296</fpage><lpage>310</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11558866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24-ndt-3-117"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Conrad</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>The meaning of medications: another look at compliance</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3975668</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25-ndt-3-117"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattson</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Prevey</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1989a</year><article-title>How often is medication taken as prescribed? A novel assessment technique</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>261</volume><fpage>3273</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2716163</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26-ndt-3-117"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>J</given-names>